{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.evenFace_shadow_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.evenFace_shadow_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EvenFaceMassShadow.lean#L113-L127","doc":"**The even face's classical shadow is a split-independent invariant.**\nCorollary of canonicity: if `qCubic = e + o = e' + o'` are two even/odd\nsplits over a characteristic-`≠ 2` field, then `φ(e) = φ(e')` for every ring\nhom `φ` — the classical mass value read off the even face does not depend on\nhow the split was presented. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.parity_decomposition_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.parity_decomposition_unique","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EvenFaceMassShadow.lean#L81-L111","doc":"**The graded split is canonical (unique).** Over a characteristic-`≠ 2`\nfield `F`, if `qCubic = e + o = e' + o'` with `e, e'` bar-even and `o, o'`\nbar-odd, then `e = e'` and `o = o'`. Proof: the difference `e − e' = o' − o`\nis simultaneously bar-even (LHS) and bar-odd (RHS), hence `2·(e − e') = 0`,\nso `e = e'` in characteristic `≠ 2`; the odd parts then agree by\ncancellation. The even/odd (mass/decay) decomposition of the q-cubic has a\nsingle well-defined home — the structural counterpart of the super-Berezinian\nblock-diagonalization. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.oddFace_shadow_null","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.oddFace_shadow_null","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EvenFaceMassShadow.lean#L70-L79","doc":"**The odd face is classically inert.** The bar-odd decay face `o` is\nannihilated by every bar-compatible evaluation into a characteristic-`≠ 2`\nfield: `φ(o) = 0`. (The `2·φ(o) = 0` division-free form is\n`oddWeight_shadow_zero`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.evenFace_carries_shadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.evenFace_carries_shadow","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EvenFaceMassShadow.lean#L58-L68","doc":"**The even face carries the whole classical shadow.** For the graded split\n`qCubic = e + o` with `e` bar-even and `o` bar-odd, every bar-compatible\nevaluation `φ` (`φ ∘ σ = φ`) into a characteristic-`≠ 2` field gives\n`φ(qCubic) = φ(e)`. The nonzero classical mass content is sourced entirely by\nthe even (C1/cosh) face. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.IsEvenFace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EvenFaceMassShadow.IsEvenFace","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EvenFaceMassShadow.lean#L52-L56","doc":"**Bar-evenness of the even/mass (C1) face.** Abbreviation matching the\nbar-even cosh profile: `σ e = e`. The bar-fixed locus is a subring\n(`ZBarParity.bar_fixed_add/mul/pow`), so a C1 kernel assembled from bar-even\natoms by ring operations stays on this face. ","signatureChunk":0}]}